.TH KANBAN 1 "October 2026" "kanban 0.1.70" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kanban \- local orchestration board for coding agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kanban
.RI [ --port " " number|auto ]
.RI [ --no-open ]
.RI [ task | hooks | update | mcp ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kanban
starts the local Kanban runtime server and serves the web UI.

When launched inside a git repository, it opens that repository's indexed workspace.
When launched outside git, it starts with no active workspace or falls back to the first indexed project.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --host <ip>
Host IP to bind the server to (default: 127.0.0.1).
.TP
.B --port <number|auto>
Runtime port (1-65535) or pick the first available port starting at 3484.
.TP
.B --no-open
Do not open the browser automatically.
.TP
.B --skip-shutdown-cleanup
Do not move sessions to done or delete task worktrees on shutdown.
.TP
.B --https
Enable HTTPS. Requires both --cert and --key.
.TP
.B --cert <path>, --key <path>
TLS certificate and private key PEM files. Both are required to serve HTTPS.
.TP
.B --update
Update Kanban to the latest published version and exit.
.TP
.B --no-passcode
Disable auto-generated passcode for remote access (for advanced users behind a reverse proxy).
.TP
.B --help, -h
Show help text and exit.
.TP
.B --version, -v
Show version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B task|tasks
Manage Kanban board tasks from the CLI.

All task commands return JSON and use kebab-case flags only. Unless
noted, each accepts
.B --project-path <path>
(workspace path; defaults to the current directory workspace).
.P
.TP
.B task list [--column <backlog|in_progress|review|done|trash>]
List the tasks for a workspace.
.TP
.BI "task create --prompt " text
Create a task in backlog. Optional:
.BR --title ,
.BR --base-ref ,
.BR --start-in-plan-mode ,
.BR --auto-review-enabled ,
.BI --auto-review-mode " " commit|pr ,
.BR --agent-id ,
.BR --cline-provider ,
.BR --cline-model ,
.BR --cline-reasoning-effort .
.TP
.BI "task update --task-id " id
Update a task's fields. Accepts the same options as create, all optional, but at least one field must be given.
.TP
.B task trash (--task-id <id> | --column <column>)
Discard a task or an entire column: move to trash, stop sessions, and clean up task workspaces (preservation-gated).
.TP
.B task complete|done (--task-id <id> | --column <column>)
Move a task or an entire column to done and stop its task session. Work is preserved and never deleted.
.TP
.BI "task locate --task-id " id
Show where a task's worktree and preserved work state live.
.TP
.BI "task review --task-id " id
Review a task in a fresh bounded session (and run the verification gate when configured); records a tree-bound verdict.
.TP
.BI "task deliver --task-id " id
Deterministically commit, integrate, push, and verify a task's work (requires gitDeliveryPolicy.enabled). Optional:
.BR --commit-message .
.TP
.BI "task delivery --task-id " id
Show a task's delivery receipt and whether its linked tasks may start.
.TP
.B task cleanup
Retry blocked worktree cleanups, remove delivered Done worktrees, and prune preserved work past retention.
.TP
.BI "task recover --task-id " id
Restore a removed task worktree from its preserved work state.
.TP
.BI "task status --task-id " id
Show aggregated task diagnostics: pipeline phase, delivery/review/dispatch state, preserved work, and context usage.
.TP
.B task queue
Show every task's reliable-completion phase (board chip data).
.TP
.B task export-diag --task-id <id> --output <file>
Download the task's full-fidelity diagnostics bundle (schemaVersion 3 JSON).
.TP
.B task delete (--task-id <id> | --column <column>)
Permanently delete a task or every task in a column.
.TP
.B task link --task-id <id> --linked-task-id <id>
Link two tasks so one task waits on another.
.TP
.BI "task unlink --dependency-id " id
Remove an existing dependency link.
.TP
.BI "task start --task-id " id
Start a task session and move task to in_progress.

.TP
.B hooks
Runtime hook helpers used by agent adapters.

Subcommands:
.br
.B ingest
.RI [ payload ]
.B --event
.RI " " to_review|to_in_progress|activity
.RI [ --source " " source ]
.RI [ --activity-text " " text ]
.RI [ --tool-name " " name ]
.RI [ --final-message " " text ]
.RI [ --hook-event-name " " name ]
.RI [ --notification-type " " type ]
.RI [ --metadata-base64 " " base64 ]
.br
.B notify
same options as
.BR ingest ,
but best-effort.
.br
.B codex-hook
.RI [ payload ]
Codex hook entrypoint (same
.B --event
options as
.BR ingest ).
.br
.B gemini-hook
.br
.B codex-wrapper
.B --real-binary
.RI " " path
.RI [ agentArgs... ]

.TP
.B update
Update Kanban to the latest published version.
.TP
.B mcp
Deprecated compatibility command. Prints a deprecation warning and exits.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start server on the default port:
.B kanban
.TP
Start server without auto-opening a browser:
.B kanban --no-open
.TP
Start server on a custom port:
.B kanban --port 9000
.TP
List tasks for the current workspace:
.B kanban task list
.TP
Create and start a task manually:
.B kanban task create --prompt "Implement API pagination"
.TP
Ingest a hook event:
.B kanban hooks ingest --event to_review
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR npm (1)
